# Every top-level subfolder is generated by run-sample.ps1 / convert-project.ps1 or is the
# old upstream clone (_upstream) / local feed - except the compatibility shims and the folders below.
/*/
# The builds' logs (FrameworkOnCore: <out>.build.log; --build-original: <out>.original.build.log).
/*.build.log
!/shims/
shims/*/bin/
shims/*/obj/
# The converter's version of FrameworkOnCore's packages for the shims (RuntimeSetup.WriteShimsVersion).
shims/FrameworkOnCoreVersion.g.props
!/icu/
icu/*/bin/
icu/*/obj/
!/casefs/
casefs/out/
casefs/test/*/bin/
casefs/test/*/obj/
!/api-probe/
api-probe/bin/
api-probe/obj/
# Three inputs of the generated folders (tests/README.md, "files a new machine needs"); the rest of each folder is generated.
# The local test SQL login of SQL Server Express (studio-verify.ps1, sample-parity.ps1): "User ID=...;Password=...".
!/_verify/
/_verify/*
!/_verify/sql-login.txt
# This machine's .NET Framework culture data (capture-culture.ps1), converted into the corpora (convert-corpora.ps1).
!/_culture/
/_culture/*
!/_culture/culture-profile.json
# Requests a page and posts its form back (n2-install.ps1).
!/_linux/
/_linux/*
!/_linux/page.ps1
# The text of doubles and floats against .NET Framework's (framework-golden.ps1 writes the golden data: generated, 110 MB).
!/numbers-parity/
numbers-parity/bin/
numbers-parity/obj/
numbers-parity/framework-golden.txt
# The branch coverage of FrameworkOnCore's runtime by the tests (measure.py, port_branches.py): the scripts; their results generated (hundreds of MB).
!/coverage/
coverage/results/
coverage/*.log
